  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 141 PM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nHigh pressure will stick around through the weekend and through\nmost of next week, keeping our weather steady state.\nSouthwesterly flow returns early next week as high pressure over\nthe SE CONUS starts to push east. This will bring down our\ntemperatures just a bit by a couple of degrees by mid-week.\nThough, temperatures will still be around 5 to 10 degrees above\nnormal for this time of year. No rain is in the forecast until\nthe end of next week, near Halloween. This is when our next\npattern change moves into the area with an incoming cold front\nbrining us widespread rainfall. Until then, highs will be in the\nmid to upper 70s with lows in the 50s with wind gusts staying\naround 15 mph or less through the next several days.",
